@page "/"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@using DxThemeVariablesExample.Models

<h1>DevExpress Design System</h1>

<p>This example illustrates how to stylize a Blazor application with use of DevExpress design system. 
DevExpress components utilize various CSS variables for their styling. To make your application's look and feel consistent you can use the same variables to style native HTML elements
or even override them to change the appearance of both: DevExpress components and native HTML elements</p>

<div class="container-with-devexpress-styles">
    <h4>Native HTML Elements</h4>

    <p> This section contains native HTML elements which use DevExpress variables for their font size, font weight, padding, and background color properties. Below are 
        examples on how to apply default DevExpress styles or override them
    </p>
    <p class="hovered"> This paragraph applies DevExpress style on hover("<strong>--dxds-color-surface-primary-default-hovered</strong>"). </p>
    <p class="utility-blue"> This paragraph applies "utility-blue" background("<strong>--dxds-color-surface-utility-blue-default-restt</strong>"). </p>
    <p class="danger"> This paragraph applies "danger" font color("<strong>--dxds-color-content-danger-default-rest</strong>"). </p>
</div>

<div>
    <h4> Local Override </h4>
    <p> You can also override DevExpress variables locally. These two buttons are both Primary buttons, but the second button's
        <strong>"--dxds-color-surface-primary-default-rest"</strong> variable is overridden locally.
    </p>
    <DxButton RenderStyle="ButtonRenderStyle.Primary" Text="Primary"></DxButton>
    <DxButton RenderStyle="ButtonRenderStyle.Primary" Text="Overridden Primary" CssClass="btn-with-custom-background"></DxButton>
</div>

<div>
    <h4> DevExpress Elements </h4>
    <p>
        The Grid header uses a DevExpress primary color <strong>("--dxds-color-surface-primary-default-rest")</strong> same as the native HTML element above, 
        and highlights hovered rows with the similar style(<strong>"--dxds-color-surface-primary-default-hovered"</strong>).
    </p>

    <DxGrid Data="Customers" CssClass="grid-with-custom-styles" HighlightRowOnHover="true" CustomizeElement="OnCustomizeElement">
        <Columns>
            <DxGridDataColumn Caption="Name" FieldName="Name" />
            <DxGridDataColumn Caption="Age" FieldName="Age" />
        </Columns>
    </DxGrid>
</div>

@code
{
    List<Customer> Customers { get; set; } = new List<Customer>() {
        new Customer() { Name = "John Smith", Age = 35 },
        new Customer() { Name = "Anne Williams", Age = 40 },
        new Customer() { Name = "Darren Park", Age = 25 }
    };
    private void OnCustomizeElement(GridCustomizeElementEventArgs args)
    {
        if (args.ElementType == GridElementType.HeaderCell)
        {
            args.CssClass = "custom-grid-header";
        }
    }
}
